{"chunk_id": "d4bf68b0e5c6", "text": "As the monkey search party despairs after failing to find Sita within the time limit set by Sugriva, they resolve to fast to death rather than face punishment. Their lament is overheard by the aged vulture Sampati, brother of the slain Jatayu. Moved by the news of his brother\u2019s death and unable to avenge him due to his burned wings, Sampati recounts how he once shielded Jatayu from the sun during a reckless flight toward it, sacrificing his own wings. Though weakened, he offers crucial knowledge: he witnessed Ravana abducting a beautiful woman crying out for Rama and Lakshmana, dropping her ornaments as she was carried away. Concluding she was Sita, Sampati reveals that Ravana dwells in the golden island-city of Lanka far across the southern sea. This revelation transforms the monkeys\u2019 despair into direction, pointing the quest toward its decisive ocean crossing.\nThe vulture Sampati recounts Jatayu\u2019s fate and reveals that Ravana carried Sita to Lanka across the southern sea.\nThemes: revelation of Sita's location, brotherly sacrifice, aging and duty, hope after despair, quest direction", "vector": [-0.007884533144533634, -0.024909963831305504, 0.01141593512147665, 0.004920193459838629, -0.010234273970127106, 0.023062769323587418, -0.014492329210042953, -0.005993196275085211, -0.03278770670294762, -0.028903163969516754, 0.016502510756254196, 0.021405726671218872, 0.008027147501707077, 0.002787770004943013, 0.0024295365437865257, -0.008971118368208408, 0.03618328645825386, -0.005208817310631275, 0.028740176931023598, -0.01753476820886135, -0.018200300633907318, 0.0007241071434691548, -0.006713058799505234, -0.004135814495384693, 0.0038709596265107393, 0.0034329299814999104, 0.00555177079513669, -0.03631910681724548, 0.012957527302205563, 0.008909998461604118, -0.011307276785373688, -0.02170453779399395, -0.019123898819088936, -0.010098450817167759, -0.017684172838926315, 0.009100150316953659, -0.009962627664208412,